{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness", "label": "Porting Superpowers to a New Harness", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_hard_requirement_session_start_injection", "label": "Hard Requirement: Automatic Session-Start Injection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single non-negotiable capability: the harness must inject the bootstrap into the model's context at the start of every session with no per-session opt-in by the human partner; if the only path is opt-in, the port is not a real port."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_capability_checklist", "label": "Harness Capability Checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Part 2 table of capabilities a harness needs to support Superpowers: skill discovery+invocation, file read/write/edit, shell commands, subagent dispatch, todo tracking, web fetch/search, and polyglot Windows script execution; each marked essential or degradable with a fallback."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_definition_of_done", "label": "Definition of Done for a Port", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Part 3: a port is finished only when the bootstrap loads every session with no opt-in, a tool mapping exists, skills are invocable, the acceptance test passes, tests cover the integration, and a real user can install it through the harness's own mechanism with the version tracked."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_acceptance_test", "label": "Acceptance Test: brainstorming auto-triggers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In a clean session the user message \"Let's make a react todo list\" must auto-trigger the brainstorming skill before any code is written; the full transcript is required for the PR."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_shape_a_shell_hook", "label": "Integration Shape A: Shell-Hook", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Harness runs a shell command at session start and reads JSON from stdout; the script reads using-superpowers/SKILL.md and prints a harness-specific JSON shape (field name and nesting differ per harness); references: hooks/session-start, hooks/run-hook.cmd, hooks/hooks.json, hooks-cursor.json."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_shape_b_in_process_plugin", "label": "Integration Shape B: In-Process Plugin/Extension", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Harness loads a JS/TS module with lifecycle callbacks; bootstrap is assembled in code (strip frontmatter, wrap in EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT, inline tool mapping) and injected as a user-role message with a dedup guard and compaction re-injection; references: .opencode/plugins/superpowers.js, .pi/extensions/superpowers.ts."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_shape_c_instructions_file", "label": "Integration Shape C: Instructions-File", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No shell hook or code plugin; the installed extension ships a manifest-declared context file (e.g. Gemini contextFileName -> GEMINI.md) that @-includes the bootstrap skill and tool-mapping reference; the harness loads it raw with no injector."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_porting_procedure", "label": "Porting Procedure (Steps 1-7)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Part 5 prescriptive procedure that branches on integration shape: study reference, create manifest/entry point, wire bootstrap injection, write tool mapping, handle no-native-skill-tool, add tests, and install locally then drive a live instance via tmux."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_distribution_channels", "label": "Distribution and Release Channels", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Part 6: per-harness distribution (marketplace, fork sync, git-URL install, package-manifest fields, local installer), plus rules that the bootstrap must be a file the installer recognizes, exec bits may be stripped so scripts are invoked via interpreter, install docs must be written, and new manifests registered in .version-bump.json."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_rule_skills_name_actions", "label": "Rule 1: Skills Name Actions, Not Tools", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Do not edit skill bodies to fit a harness; a port only adds a tool-mapping reference and a bootstrap injector and never reaches into skills/*/SKILL.md to swap tool names, because skill content is behavior-shaping code."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_rule_ship_via_install_mechanism", "label": "Rule 2: Ship Through the Harness's Own Install Mechanism", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The bootstrap, skills, and tool mapping are delivered as part of what the harness installs (plugin/extension/marketplace entry); a port must never hand-edit the user's global or personal config files to inject anything."}, {"id": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_windows_polyglot_hook", "label": "Windows / Polyglot Hook (run-hook.cmd)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Part 7: hooks/run-hook.cmd is a polyglot valid as both Windows batch and Unix shell; enforces that hook scripts are extensionless (a .sh would be double-invoked by Claude Code's Windows handling) and that there is one extensionless bash script plus the wrapper for all three platforms."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness", "target": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_hard_requirement_session_start_injection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness", "target": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_capability_checklist", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness", "target": "docs_porting_to_a_new_harness_definition_of_done", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/porting-to-a-new-harness.md", "source_location": n